futures and forward markets. The net asset value per Unit would have increased by $50.00, $20.00
from the increase in the per ounce price of gold and $30.00 from interest and speculative trading,
and would be $950.00 or approximately 1.032 ounces of gold (950 &#247; 920). <I>The foregoing example is
for illustrative purposes only. There can be no assurance, that the U.S. dollar price of gold will
rise or not decline or that a Series will not incur losses from its futures and forward trading.
The U.S. dollar price for gold established at the London A.M. fixing, and the closing price for the
gold futures contracts to be traded by the Series will normally be different from each other,
