</DIV>


<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Within each Series, Units will be issued in two sub-Series. Series&nbsp;A-1 Units and Series&nbsp;B-1
Units are subject to the selling commissions described below.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Series&nbsp;A and Series&nbsp;B will pay Superfund Asset Management, Inc. a selling commission of 4% of
the average month-end net asset value of each outstanding Series&nbsp;A-1 Unit and Series&nbsp;B-1 Unit,
respectively, in monthly installments of 1/12 of 4% of the month end net asset value of such Units
(the liability for which will be allocated to the Series&nbsp;A-1 Units and Series&nbsp;B-1 Units, not Series
A and Series&nbsp;B generally). However, pursuant to NASD Rule&nbsp;2810(b)(4)(B)(i) pertaining to maximum
allowable selling commissions, the maximum cumulative selling commission per Unit is 10% of the
initial public offering price for such Unit. See &#147;Charges &#151; Sales Compensation.&#148;
</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Series&nbsp;A-2 Units and Series&nbsp;B-2 Units are not subject to selling commissions but are available
only to investors participating in selling agent asset-based or fixed-fee investment programs or a
registered investment adviser&#146;s asset-based fee or fixed fee advisory program through which an
investment adviser recommends a portfolio allocation to the Fund and for which Superfund Asset
Management, Inc. or an affiliate serves as selling agent. Subject to NASD Rule&nbsp;2810(b)(4)(B)(i)
pertaining to maximum allowable selling commissions, the General Partner, not the Series or any
Limited Partner, may pay certain broker-dealers an administrative fee of up to 0.50% of the average
annual Net Asset Value of the outstanding Series&nbsp;A-2 Units and Series&nbsp;B-2 Units sold by such
broker-dealers or through such broker-dealers&#146; investment fund platforms.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Once a Series&nbsp;A-1 Unit or Series&nbsp;B-1 Unit has been charged selling commissions totaling 10% of
the sale price of such Unit, the Unit will not be charged any further selling commissions and the
net asset value of such Unit will be recalculated, and the Unit will be redesignated, in terms of
Series&nbsp;A-2 Units or Series&nbsp;B-2 Units, as applicable, against which selling commissions are not
charged. The redesignation of Series&nbsp;A-1 Units to Series&nbsp;A-2 or Series&nbsp;B-1 Units to Series&nbsp;B-2
Units will have no impact on the net asset value of an investor&#146;s investment in the Fund at the
time of such redesignation.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The General Partner and Superfund Asset Management, Inc. may retain additional selling agents
to assist with the placement of the Units. Superfund Asset Management Inc. will pay all or a
portion of the annual selling commission it receives in respect of the Units sold by the additional
selling agents to the additional selling agents effecting the sales.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Superfund Asset Management, Inc. may engage one or more registered broker-dealers to solicit
other broker-dealers to become selling agents and to assist those selling agents with the offering
and sale of the Units, that is, to act as wholesalers. As compensation for its services, any such
wholesaler will receive up to one-fourth of the selling commission that would otherwise be paid to
the selling agents. Thus a wholesaler may receive up to 1% of the average month-end net asset
value per Unit in the initial year after purchase of such Unit, and additional selling commissions
of up to 1% per annum of the month-end net asset value per Unit thereafter, limited, when combined
with payments made in the first year, to 2.5% of the proceeds of the sale of such Unit.
</DIV>

