<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 12pt"><U><B>A Gold Denominated Investment</B></U>
</DIV>


<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Gold has often been viewed as a hedge against inflation and thus as a safe haven in troubled
or uncertain economic times. Gold has also been used as a hedge against fluctuations in the value
of the U.S. dollar against other currencies. Historically, when the dollar has depreciated against
foreign currencies generally, the dollar price of gold has risen, and vice versa.
</DIV>

<DIV align="left" style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 6pt">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Superfund
Gold, L.P. is designed to combine an investment in gold with an investment in a managed
futures strategy. The gold investment of each Series is intended to de-link the Series&#146; net asset
value, which is denominated in U.S. dollars, from the value of the U.S. dollar relative to gold,
essentially denominating the Series&#146; net asset value in terms of gold. <I>However, if the U.S. dollar
value of gold declines resulting in dollar losses for the Series, there can</I>
